.\" sessionintent.1
.\" Manual page for sessionintent
.\"
.TH SESSIONINTENT 1 "2026-02-27" "sessionintent 0.2.0" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
sessionintent \- A declarative session orchestration system for GNOME Wayland

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sessionintent
[\fIOPTION\fR]...

.SH DESCRIPTION
SessionIntent is a session orchestration system for GNOME Wayland that allows
you to switch between different "intent-based modes" that automatically launch,
reuse, and organize your applications across workspaces.

.SH OPTIONS

.SS "Mode Selection"
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-mode \fIMODE\fR
Apply a specific mode directly, bypassing the UI selector.

.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-prompt
Prompt for mode selection via UI (requires wofi or rofi).
This is the default behavior when no arguments are provided.

.SS "Session Control"
.TP
.BR \-P ", " \-\-panic
Clear current session state without killing any processes.

.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quit
Gracefully close managed applications (sends SIGTERM).

.TP
.BR \-\-clear
Clear state files only (without touching applications).

.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-kill
Force kill managed applications (sends SIGKILL).

.TP
.BR \-S ", " \-\-suspend
Suspend session (pause mode switching).

.SS "Information"
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-status
Show current session status (mode, power state, dev mode).

.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-list
List available modes from configuration.

.SS "Configuration"
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-init
Initialize default configuration files.

.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-reload
Reload configuration files.

.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config \fIPATH\fR
Use a custom configuration file instead of the default.

.SS "Developer"
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-dev
Enable developer mode: print commands instead of executing them.

.SS "Miscellaneous"
.TP
.BR \-\-help
Display this help message and exit.

.TP
.BR \-\-version
Display version information and exit.

.SH EXAMPLES
.SS "Basic Usage"
.TP
.I "sessionintent"
Select a session mode using the UI (default behavior).

.TP
.I "sessionintent -m work"
Apply the 'work' mode directly.

.TP
.I "sessionintent -d -m work"
See what commands would be executed without running them.

.SS "Session Control"
.TP
.I "sessionintent -P"
Clear the current session state.

.TP
.I "sessionintent -q"
Gracefully close all managed applications.

.TP
.I "sessionintent -k"
Force kill all managed applications.

.TP
.I "sessionintent -S"
Suspend the current session.

.SS "Information"
.TP
.I "sessionintent -s"
Show current session status.

.TP
.I "sessionintent -l"
List all available modes.

.SS "Configuration"
.TP
.I "sessionintent -i"
Initialize default configuration files.

.TP
.I "sessionintent -r"
Reload configuration files.

.SH CONFIGURATION
See the configuration guide for details on setting up modes and apps.

Configuration files are located in:
.IP
~/.config/sessionintent/config.yaml
.br
~/.config/sessionintent/apps.yaml

.SH REQUIREMENTS
.IP
\- Python 3.10+
.IP
\- PyYAML
.IP
\- wofi or rofi (for UI selection)
.IP
\- GNOME Wayland session

